<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendices</h2>

<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Multi-Agent Planner</h2>

<figure id="A1.F10" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatright" style="width:55%;"><img src="2509.13095v1/planner.png" id="A1.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:299/210;" width="299" height="210" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 10: </span>
The multi-agent planner in SeqWM.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Planning Process</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Figure <a href="#A1.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ Appendix A Multi-Agent Planner ‣ Empowering Multi-Robot Cooperation via Sequential World Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, at timestep <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the action planning process for agent <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> can be divided into the following steps:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">S1 - Communication.</span>
Agents are organized to exchange messages in a sequential manner.
Specifically, agent <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> receives a message <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{i}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{i}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> that aggregates the predicted latent states and planned actions from all its predecessors:</p>
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{i}_{t}=\begin{cases}\emptyset,&amp;i=1,\\
\bigoplus_{j&lt;i}\left(\hat{z}^{j}_{t},a^{j}_{t}\right),&amp;i&gt;1,\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{i}_{t}=\begin{cases}\emptyset,&amp;i=1,\\
\bigoplus_{j&lt;i}\left(\hat{z}^{j}_{t},a^{j}_{t}\right),&amp;i&gt;1,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\oplus" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊕</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\oplus</annotation></semantics></math> denotes concatenation.
To implement this efficiently, we employ a masking-based concatenation scheme: a fixed-length vector of dimension <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\times(|\mathcal{A}|+d_{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\times(|\mathcal{A}|+d_{z})</annotation></semantics></math> is pre-allocated, where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of agents, <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{A}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{A}|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> are the action and latent dimensions.
Agent <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> maintains an empty message, while subsequent agents sequentially fill in their designated slots with their own predictions <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{z}^{i}_{t},a^{i}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{z}^{i}_{t},a^{i}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> in addition to forwarding the received content.
This design ensures that information is progressively accumulated along the communication chain with linear complexity in the number of agents.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">S2 - Action Sampling.</span>
The planner samples <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> candidate action sequences from two sources.
We sample <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> candidate action sequences from a diagonal Gaussian distribution <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a^{i}_{t:t+H}\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mu^{i}_{t:t+H},(\sigma^{i}_{t:t+H})^{2}I\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>I</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{i}_{t:t+H}\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mu^{i}_{t:t+H},(\sigma^{i}_{t:t+H})^{2}I\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu^{i}_{t:t+H},\sigma^{i}_{t:t+H}\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{A}|\times H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{i}_{t:t+H},\sigma^{i}_{t:t+H}\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{A}|\times H}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the mean and standard deviation of the <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>-step horizon actions.
Additionally, we sample <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> action sequences directly from the actor module <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{a}^{i}_{h}\sim\pi^{i,\textrm{Act}}(\cdot|o^{i}_{h},e^{i}_{h}),h=t:t+H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Act</mtext></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}^{i}_{h}\sim\pi^{i,\textrm{Act}}(\cdot|o^{i}_{h},e^{i}_{h}),h=t:t+H</annotation></semantics></math>, and combine these two sets of action sequences to form <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> candidate action sequences.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">S3 - World Model Prediction.</span>
Following sampling, the world model predicts <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>-step trajectories for each sampled action sequence using Eq. (<a href="#S4.E2" title="In 4.1 Sequential Multi-Agent World Model ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ Empowering Multi-Robot Cooperation via Sequential World Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), generating <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> predicted sequences <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Gamma=\{(\hat{z}^{i}_{h},a^{i}_{h},\hat{r}^{i}_{h})\}_{h=t:t+H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma=\{(\hat{z}^{i}_{h},a^{i}_{h},\hat{r}^{i}_{h})\}_{h=t:t+H}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">S4 - Value Evaluation.</span>
Each predicted trajectory is assigned a value via the <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>-step return, combining the short-term cumulative predicted reward with the terminal value from the critic:</p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{i}_{\Gamma}=\gamma^{H}Q^{i}(\hat{z}^{i}_{t+H},a^{i}_{t+H},e^{i}_{t+H})+\sum_{h=t}^{t+H-1}\gamma^{h-t}\hat{r}^{i}_{h}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>H</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{i}_{\Gamma}=\gamma^{H}Q^{i}(\hat{z}^{i}_{t+H},a^{i}_{t+H},e^{i}_{t+H})+\sum_{h=t}^{t+H-1}\gamma^{h-t}\hat{r}^{i}_{h}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">S5 - Action Optimization.</span>
The candidate action sequences are ranked by their evaluated values, and the top <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> are chosen as the elite set <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The parameters of the action distribution are updated based on the elite set using:</p>
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E8X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu^{i,(k+1)}_{t:t+H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu^{i,(k+1)}_{t:t+H}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{m=1}^{M}\alpha_{m}\Gamma_{m}^{*}}{\sum_{m=1}^{M}\alpha_{m}},\ \ \ \ \sigma^{i,(k+1)}_{t:t+H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{m=1}^{M}\alpha_{m}\Gamma_{m}^{*}}{\sum_{m=1}^{M}\alpha_{m}},\ \ \ \ \sigma^{i,(k+1)}_{t:t+H}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8X.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sqrt{\frac{\sum_{m=1}^{M}\alpha_{m}\left(\Gamma_{m}^{*}-\mu^{i,(k+1)}_{t:t+H}\right)^{2}}{\sum_{m=1}^{M}\alpha_{m}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sqrt{\frac{\sum_{m=1}^{M}\alpha_{m}\left(\Gamma_{m}^{*}-\mu^{i,(k+1)}_{t:t+H}\right)^{2}}{\sum_{m=1}^{M}\alpha_{m}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.3" class="ltx_p">where the weights are generated based on the evaluated values as <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{m}=\exp\left[\tau\left(V_{\Gamma_{m}^{*}}-\max_{m\in M}V_{\Gamma_{m}^{*}}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{m}=\exp\left[\tau\left(V_{\Gamma_{m}^{*}}-\max_{m\in M}V_{\Gamma_{m}^{*}}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> being the temperature coefficient.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Iteration.</span>
For the default setting, the above process are iterated <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> times to derive the final action distribution.
If the early-stopping heuristic is applied, after each iteration, we check whether the action optimization has converged by evaluating the KL divergence between the current and previous action distributions, <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{D}_{KL}(\mathcal{N}^{(k+1)}\|\mathcal{N}^{(k)})&lt;\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}_{KL}(\mathcal{N}^{(k+1)}\|\mathcal{N}^{(k)})&lt;\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is a small threshold.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">The detailed hyperparameters used in the model-based planner are summarized in Table <a href="#A2.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ B.4 Hyperparameters ‣ Appendix B Implementation Details ‣ Empowering Multi-Robot Cooperation via Sequential World Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Low-Pass Action Smoothing</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In real-world robotics, high-frequency changes in control inputs can cause severe mechanical impacts, accelerating wear and reducing execution stability.
Therefore, many studies in reinforcement learning and motion planning incorporate action-smoothing constraints, such as adding penalties on differences between consecutive actions during policy updates <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aractingi et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Christmann et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, introducing regularization in policy networks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2024b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, or filtering noise in trajectory optimization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pinneri et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vlahov et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kicki, 2025</a>)</cite>, to reduce jitter and improve executability.
Inspired by these methods, we apply frequency-domain low-pass filtering directly to the sampled action noise in our planner, explicitly suppressing the high-frequency components of the actions.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F11" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.13095v1/low-pass.svg" id="A1.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:543/170;" width="543" height="170"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>
Visualization of the low-pass filter.
(<span id="A1.F11.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Left</span>): Amplitude–frequency response of the low-pass filter.
(<span id="A1.F11.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Middle</span>): Filtering effects on random signals at 20% cutoff ratios, the different colors represent different action dimensions.
(<span id="A1.F11.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Right</span>): Effects of low-pass filtering on control commands in the <span id="A1.F11.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PushBox</span> task, with different colors representing different agents.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Specifically, during action sampling, we first sample noise from a standard normal distribution, apply low-pass filtering, and then add the filtered noise to the action mean to generate candidate action sequences.
We use a Butterworth filter with <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{\mathrm{LBF}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>LBF</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{\mathrm{LBF}}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, whose transfer function and amplitude–frequency response are given by:</p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(s)=\frac{2\pi f_{c}}{s+2\pi f_{c}},\quad|H(f)|=\frac{f_{c}}{\sqrt{f^{2}+f_{c}^{2}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(s)=\frac{2\pi f_{c}}{s+2\pi f_{c}},\quad|H(f)|=\frac{f_{c}}{\sqrt{f^{2}+f_{c}^{2}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> is the low-pass cutoff frequency.
As show in Figure <a href="#A1.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ A.2 Low-Pass Action Smoothing ‣ Appendix A Multi-Agent Planner ‣ Empowering Multi-Robot Cooperation via Sequential World Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, the amplitude–frequency response shows that the high-frequency components are exponentially attenuated (approaching linear decay in logarithmic coordinates).
The corresponding discrete-time difference equation, obtained via bilinear transformation, is</p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y[t]=\frac{1-\beta}{2}(x[t]+x[t-1])-\beta y[t-1],\quad\beta=\frac{1-\tan\left(\nicefrac{{\pi f_{c}}}{{f_{s}}}\right)}{1+\tan\left(\nicefrac{{\pi f_{c}}}{{f_{s}}}\right)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mi mathsize="0.700em">π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">c</mi></msub></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mi mathsize="0.700em">π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">c</mi></msub></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y[t]=\frac{1-\beta}{2}(x[t]+x[t-1])-\beta y[t-1],\quad\beta=\frac{1-\tan\left(\nicefrac{{\pi f_{c}}}{{f_{s}}}\right)}{1+\tan\left(\nicefrac{{\pi f_{c}}}{{f_{s}}}\right)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is the sampling frequency, i.e., the frequency of the control signal.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Pseudocode</h3>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Model Training</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> replay buffer <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, parameterized networks <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{E},\theta_{D},\theta_{R},\theta_{Q}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{E},\theta_{D},\theta_{R},\theta_{Q},</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> for encoder, dynamics predictor, reward predictor, critic, and actor, respectively;

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> episode <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=1,2,3,\dots," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=1,2,3,\dots,</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> step <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,2,3,\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,2,3,\dots</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
               Get real data <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="([o^{i}_{t}]_{i=1:n},[a^{i}_{t}]_{i=1:n},r_{t},[o^{i}_{t+1}]_{i=1:n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">([o^{i}_{t}]_{i=1:n},[a^{i}_{t}]_{i=1:n},r_{t},[o^{i}_{t+1}]_{i=1:n})</annotation></semantics></math> by interacting with the environment

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
               Add transition into buffer: <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{B}=\mathcal{B}\cup([o^{i}_{t}]_{i=1:n},[a^{i}_{t}]_{i=1:n},r_{t},[o^{i}_{t+1}]_{i=1:n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}=\mathcal{B}\cup([o^{i}_{t}]_{i=1:n},[a^{i}_{t}]_{i=1:n},r_{t},[o^{i}_{t+1}]_{i=1:n})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> epoch <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=1,2,3,\dots," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=1,2,3,\dots,</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
               Sample trajectories from <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
               Update <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{E},\theta_{D},\theta_{R},\theta_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{E},\theta_{D},\theta_{R},\theta_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> by minimizing Eq. (<a href="#S4.E3" title="In 4.1 Sequential Multi-Agent World Model ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ Empowering Multi-Robot Cooperation via Sequential World Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
               Update <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> by minimizing Eq. (<a href="#S4.E4" title="In 4.1 Sequential Multi-Agent World Model ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ Empowering Multi-Robot Cooperation via Sequential World Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Model Planning</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> learned parameters <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{E},\theta_{D},\theta_{R},\theta_{Q},\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{E},\theta_{D},\theta_{R},\theta_{Q},\psi</annotation></semantics></math>,
hyperparameters <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H,K,\tau,N_{p},M,N_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H,K,\tau,N_{p},M,N_{a}</annotation></semantics></math>, initial distribution;

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> step <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,2,3,\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,2,3,\dots</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> agent <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
               Get environment observation <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{i}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{i}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and encode it to latent space: <math id="alg2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{i}_{t}=E^{i}(o^{i}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{i}_{t}=E^{i}(o^{i}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
               <span id="alg2.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
                 Retrieve the message from the previous agent <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{i}_{t}=\bigoplus_{j&lt;i}\left(\hat{z}^{j}_{t},a^{j}_{t}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{i}_{t}=\bigoplus_{j&lt;i}\left(\hat{z}^{j}_{t},a^{j}_{t}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
               <span id="alg2.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
                 set <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{i}_{t}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{i}_{t}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
               <span id="alg2.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
               <span id="alg2.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> iteration <math id="alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=1,2,3,\dots,K_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=1,2,3,\dots,K_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
                 Sample <math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> actions <math id="alg2.l11.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a^{i}_{t:t+H}\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mu^{i}_{t:t+H},{(\sigma^{i}_{t:t+H})}^{2}I\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>I</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{i}_{t:t+H}\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mu^{i}_{t:t+H},{(\sigma^{i}_{t:t+H})}^{2}I\right)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
                 Sample <math id="alg2.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> actions from actor <math id="alg2.l12.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{a}^{i}_{h}\sim\pi^{i,\textrm{Act}}(\cdot|o^{i}_{h},e^{i}_{h}),h=t:t+H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Act</mtext></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}^{i}_{h}\sim\pi^{i,\textrm{Act}}(\cdot|o^{i}_{h},e^{i}_{h}),h=t:t+H</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
                 Get predictions by world model rollouts, <math id="alg2.l13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Gamma=\{(\hat{z}^{i}_{h},a^{i}_{h},\hat{r}^{i}_{h})\}_{h=t:t+H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma=\{(\hat{z}^{i}_{h},a^{i}_{h},\hat{r}^{i}_{h})\}_{h=t:t+H}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
                 Evaluate the trajectories by Eq. (<a href="#A1.E7" title="In A.1 Planning Process ‣ Appendix A Multi-Agent Planner ‣ Empowering Multi-Robot Cooperation via Sequential World Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) and select top-<math id="alg2.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> elite action sequences

</div>
<div id="alg2.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
                 Update action distribution following Eq. (<a href="#A1.E8" title="In A.1 Planning Process ‣ Appendix A Multi-Agent Planner ‣ Empowering Multi-Robot Cooperation via Sequential World Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>)

</div>
<div id="alg2.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
               <span id="alg2.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F12" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.13095v1/implement.svg" id="A2.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:543/159;" width="543" height="159"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 12: </span>
Overview of implementation details.
(<span id="A2.F12.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Left</span>): SEM Normalization.
(<span id="A2.F12.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Middle</span>): Symlog transformation, where the <math id="A2.F12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>-axis represents the values encoded by two-hot encoding, and the <math id="A2.F12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>-axis represents the values aligned with the scalar target.
(<span id="A2.F12.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Right</span>): Normalized <math id="A2.F12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>-scale and return in the <span id="A2.F12.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Dex-BottleCap</span> task.
</figcaption>
